menu "Reed-Solomon code"

    config RS_IN_RAM
        bool "Place code and data in IRAM"
        default n
        help
            Speed up.

    config RS_GMUL_IN_RAM
        bool "Place the multiplication table gmul (64 KB) in DRAM"
        depends on RS_IN_RAM
        default y
        help
            The 256x256 multiplication table of GF(256) takes 65536 bytes. With this option it is
            kept in internal RAM like the other tables. Without it the table stays in flash and is
            read through the cache, which frees 64 KB of internal RAM. Only decode() reads the
            table (the syndromes, Berlekamp-Massey, the Chien search and Forney); encode() works
            with remTable and does not depend on this option.

    config RS_PIE
        bool "Use PIE (SIMD) instructions of ESP32-S3"
        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
        default n
        help
            The division by the generator polynomial keeps its 16-byte remainder in one
            128-bit Q register: a step costs one vector load of remTable[x] and one vector
            XOR instead of 16 byte loads, XORs and stores. Speeds up encode() and, to a
            lesser extent, decode(). The encoded and decoded data is the same as without
            this option.

endmenu
